        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "When Martians read nursery rhymes"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "A funny play about Martians who want to invade Earth and make a big mistake."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "Think-Tank and Noodle",
          "misreading the book",
          "moral",
          "the Martians",
          "the joke",
          "the retreat",
          "the space probe",
          "wrong conclusions"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "The play is by Claire Boiko. Martians Think-Tank and Noodle plan to invade Earth.\nThink-Tank is vain, and admires his big brain in a mirror. Noodle is his obedient assistant.\nThey send a space probe to Earth to collect information and find a book.\nThe Martians cannot understand the book. They think the nursery rhymes in it are a code for secret information.\nThey think it shows the Earth's secret weapons and the Earth people's plans.\nFrightened, they cancel the invasion and turn back.\nThe play is a comedy. The book that saved the Earth is only a book of nursery rhymes.\nIt shows how arrogance and misunderstanding can defeat a mighty plan."
        }
